>
> Subscripts appear to be more a fairly general means of attaching  
> additional information or distinctions to grammatical words, rather  
> than a representation of the typographical practice of subscripting.

The meaning of zo xi is analogous to the mathematical practice of  
subscripting. In mathematics superscripts are variously used for lo  
tenfa, repetitions of other elements than multiplication, and in ways  
similar to subscripts.

